        "original_id": "6b3773a2-2687-519c-b5e6-c13528660d54",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships\n- Organizations: Asian Athletics Association\n- Sports/Disciplines: 3000 metres steeplechase, track and field steeplechase\n- People: Mekdes Bekele Tadese\n\nFacts:\n- The 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships was the ninth edition of an international athletics competition for Asian under-20 athletes.\n- The Asian Athletics Association organised the 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships.\n- A total of 43 events were contested at the 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships.\n- The events at the 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships were divided equally between male and female athletes except for the men's 3000 metres steeplechase.\n- The 3000 metres steeplechase is the most common steeplechase distance in track and field.\n- The 3000 metres steeplechase is an obstacle race run over 3000 metres.\n- The name of the 3000 metres steeplechase derives from the horse racing steeplechase.\n- Mekdes Bekele Tadese, born on 20 January 1987, is an Ethiopian runner who specializes in the 3000 metres steeplechase.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c8375797-5214-58e2-a503-9e1bfcec8ec2",
        "text": "Page: 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships. Sentence: The 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships was the ninth edition of the international athletics competition for Asian under-20 athletes, organised by the Asian Athletics Association.\nPage: 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships. Sentence: A total of 43 events were contested, which were divided equally between male and female athletes aside from the men's 3000 metres steeplechase.\nPage: 3000 metres steeplechase. Sentence: The 3000 metres steeplechase or 3000-meter steeplechase is the most common distance for the steeplechase in track and field.\nPage: 3000 metres steeplechase. Sentence: It is an obstacle race over the distance of the 3000 metres, which derives its name from the horse racing steeplechase.\nPage: Mekdes Bekele. Sentence: Mekdes Bekele Tadese (Amharic: መቅደስ በቀለ ታደሰ; born 20 January 1987) is an Ethiopian runner who specializes in the 3000 metres steeplechase.",
